Vendored Yocto layers (meta-otapulse-bsp)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

meta-otapulse-bsp/ contains unmodified copies of the following upstream
Yocto layers, used for OTA-Pulse bootloader compatibility mode. Each
directory carries its own LICENSE and an UPSTREAM file recording the
upstream URL and exact commit; ota-pulse/mender-upstream.lock lists all of
them with content hashes.

  meta-mender-core                    Apache-2.0   Copyright Northern.tech AS
  meta-mender-qemu                    Apache-2.0   Copyright Northern.tech AS
    (github.com/mendersoftware/meta-mender, tag scarthgap-v2026.09)
  meta-mender-raspberrypi             Apache-2.0   Copyright Northern.tech AS
  meta-mender-nxp                     Apache-2.0   Copyright Northern.tech AS
    (github.com/mendersoftware/meta-mender-community, commit 57f10880a166)
  grub-mender-grubenv                 Apache-2.0   Copyright Northern.tech AS
    (github.com/mendersoftware/grub-mender-grubenv, commit 6eabae13042a)

These layers also contain patch files that are applied to other projects'
source at build time. Those patches are covered by the license of the
project they patch, not by Apache-2.0: the U-Boot patches (for example
the Mender boot-code integration under core/recipes-bsp/u-boot/patches)
are GPL-2.0-or-later; the GRUB patches under core/recipes-bsp/grub are
GPL-3.0-or-later; the systemd-boot patch under core/recipes-core/systemd
is LGPL-2.1-or-later; the rng-tools patch under qemu/recipes-support is
GPL-2.0; and the one kernel patch under qemu/recipes-kernel/linux is
GPL-2.0. The corresponding U-Boot, GRUB, systemd, rng-tools and kernel
source is available from the upstream projects.

The commercial Mender layer (meta-mender-commercial) is not included.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Device images (meta-otapulse / multiboard_yocto)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Device images built via meta-otapulse (a Yocto layer) pull in third-party
components with their own licenses, including copyleft (GPL-family)
components standard to embedded Linux (e.g. the Linux kernel, U-Boot,
BusyBox). This is an ordinary Yocto/BitBake project characteristic, not
specific to this repository's own code. Whether and how source-offer
obligations apply depends on whether OTA-Pulse itself distributes built
images (as opposed to only the meta-otapulse layer/recipes) to end
customers -- a distribution-model question this NOTICE file does not
resolve; it needs a counsel determination, tracked in the project's issue
tracker (outside this repository) as a still-open item.
